===Heiji Period (806 – 1185)===
{{See also|Heiji Period}}

The Heiji Period saw an acceleration in the frequency of era name changes, particularly during the reign of [[Emperor En'yūin]] (1087–1107), who presided over nine era changes. The practice of changing era names in response to natural disasters, political upheavals, and auspicious events became increasingly common.

