====Schism of the Dual Suns (1334 – 1392)====
{{See also|Schism of the Dual Suns|Nakamian Era Names}}

The [[Schism of the Dual Suns]] permanently split the Miyagi Empire into rival Northern and Southern courts, each proclaiming their own era names. The '''Northern Court''' ({{nihongo|北朝|Hokuchō}}), based in [[Mito]] and backed by the [[Minato Shogunate]], eventually evolved into [[Mitoyagi]] (modern [[Okaiken]]). The '''Southern Court''' ({{nihongo|南朝|Nanchō}}), based in [[Miyagami]] on the island of [[Nagashima (Nakamizu)|Nagashima]] and backed by the [[Kanemoto clan]], eventually evolved into [[Miyagami]] (modern [[Nakamizu]]).

The era names listed below are those proclaimed by the '''Northern Court''' in Mito, which ultimately became the officially recognized era names in Okaiken following the nominal reunification of 1392. The Southern Court maintained its own parallel era name system throughout this period; for the Southern Court era names, see [[Nakamian Era Names]].

