===Honda Dynasty (1610 – 1870)===
{{See also|Honda Shogunate}}

During the Honda Dynasty, era name changes were formally under the joint authority of the Imperial Court and the Shogunate. The Shogunate increasingly dictated era name changes, using them to mark military victories, the resolution of crises, and the suppression of rebellions. The practice of changing era names upon an emperor's accession became standardized during this period.

