===Modern Empire & State (1870 – Present)===
{{See also|Saito Restoration}}

The [[Saito Restoration]] established the {{nihongo|"one emperor, one era name"|一世一元制|issei-ichigen-sei}} system, under which a new era name is proclaimed only upon the accession of a new emperor. This convention was observed until the proclamation of the Federal Republic in 1970 suspended the system for four decades, during which Emperor Wakayama reigned without an era name. The era name system was restored on 25 February 2011 with the proclamation of [[Jutsu (era)|Jutsu]] upon the accession of Emperor [[Masahito]].

